{"id": "R-MEM-4", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "The evidence atom is a rolling Cell: consecutive messages (m[i], m[i+1]) on one branch path, sliding by one, recording direction (human->model or model->human); quote spans stay inside one half of a Cell", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261115-17", "rationale": "D2: \"these should be rolling cells, i.e. call response pairs that do overlap\" (Zach 2026-11-15 11:03 CT, decision sheet answers (HO-KAI-20261115-936P)); pair-and-direction form is the coordinator's reading R1, unconfirmed", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-MEM-5", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "committed", "text": "Every Cell records platform and model (when the source has them); family means model family, so cross-family links are a filter", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261115-17", "rationale": "D5 confirmed: \"4, yes\" (Zach 2026-11-15 11:03 CT, decision sheet answers (HO-KAI-20261115-936P)); committed when Zach merges this revision", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-MEM-6", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Local and provider embeddings sit behind one Embedder interface; every vector row records its model id, so a re-embed is a new index; full text, vectors and provenance are kept on Kairos's side", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261115-17", "rationale": "D3: \"test local ... I also am okay and authorizing using OpenAI's embeddings ... with pretty much full retention\" (Zach 2026-11-15 11:03 CT, decision sheet answers (HO-KAI-20261115-936P)); retention meaning is the coordinator's reading R2, unconfirmed", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-FIX-1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Benchmark fixtures are generated from readable outlines (benchmark/outlines) by benchmark/fixturegen.py; committed fixtures must equal the generator's output, gold names units by the rescued core's message_unit_id, and every fixture is synthetic text written for this repo", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261116-21", "rationale": "Fixture plan step 1 (docs/design/benchmark-fixture-plan.md: 'Fixtures are generated by a small script from a readable outline, so a reviewer edits the outline, not the JSON'); serves R-EVAL-1's per-layer scoring. Built for HO-ANA-20261116-CFNM (dry-lane dispatch, Zach 2026-11-16 15:22 CT: \"Lanes shouldn't be dry\"); the plan itself is still proposed", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-ENG-1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "The engine package (anamnesis/) imports the Python standard library only and depends on no instance: parsing, message units, rolling Cells, the FTS5 index and the Embedder interface run offline with no provider SDK installed", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261118-19", "author_role": "implementer", "rationale": "HO-ANA-20261118-6H0J item 1 (DEC-252; Zach 2026-11-18 10:52 CT: Anamnesis is the engine, an instance is made by init, the engine depends on no instance: \"correct\"); pipeline reconciliation section 4 item 4 (offline path must import without tiktoken/openai). Tested by tests/test_engine_core.py ImportTests", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-ENG-2", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Search is message-level and branch-aware: every hit names its message_unit_id and the unit's true branch_status, alternate-only text is findable but never labelled active, a snippet comes from one unit only, and query text cannot inject FTS5 syntax", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261118-19", "author_role": "implementer", "rationale": "HO-ANA-20261118-6H0J item 1 (message-level, branch-aware FTS5 index); fixture gold checks F-10 hit_resolves_to_unit, F-11 alternate_findable, F-12 snippet_single_unit (R-FIX-1). Tested by tests/test_engine_core.py IndexGoldTests", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "R-FIX-1@1"}]}
{"id": "R-ENG-3", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "The engine depends on no instance: an instance is a folder created or completed in place by `anamnesis init`, holding a validated manifest (sources, embedder, shelves, privacy), the claim ledger, rendered Frames, Films and saga, library/ and run records; init never overwrites, moves or deletes an existing file, writes nothing outside the given path, and a demo instance is built from the synthetic fixtures only", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261118-23", "author_role": "implementer", "rationale": "HO-ANA-20261118-6H0J item 2 (Zach 2026-11-18 10:52 CT: engine is Anamnesis, an instance is made by init, the engine depends on no instance: \"correct\"; DEC-252). Tested by tests/test_instance.py", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "R-ENG-1@1"}]}
{"id": "R-DCK-1", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Identical permitted inputs, pinned code, normalization version, and input manifest produce byte-identical reports.", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "rationale": "relay-kit-private kate-replies:replies/HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1--6b3fa1a21995.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T01:56:56Z), ask 6b3fa1a21995 on HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1; targets Anamnesis#13 at b2428c1. Kate's own label: 'provisional, schema-neutral drafts derived from the supplied task, not additions to Zach's authorization'; she had the handoff only, not the source. Committed verbatim by claude:anamnesis#wake-20261118-02; not accepted by Zach. Kate's id: comparator-independent-01. Kate's acceptance text: \"Repeat runs compare byte-for-byte; reports identify all pins. Ungranted inputs and unsupported normalization versions stop processing.\"", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-DCK-2", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Missing evidence, unreadable evidence, unsupported cases, and reconstructed replies remain distinguishable. A reconstruction never counts as the lost original.", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "rationale": "relay-kit-private kate-replies:replies/HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1--6b3fa1a21995.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T01:56:56Z), ask 6b3fa1a21995 on HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1; targets Anamnesis#13 at b2428c1. Kate's own label: 'provisional, schema-neutral drafts derived from the supplied task, not additions to Zach's authorization'; she had the handoff only, not the source. Committed verbatim by claude:anamnesis#wake-20261118-02; not accepted by Zach. Kate's id: comparator-independent-02. Kate's acceptance text: \"Independent fixtures cover each distinction, including a byte-identical declared reconstruction.\"", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-DCK-3", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Each classified row retains traceable evidence locators and keeps event times distinct from observation time.", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "rationale": "relay-kit-private kate-replies:replies/HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1--6b3fa1a21995.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T01:56:56Z), ask 6b3fa1a21995 on HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1; targets Anamnesis#13 at b2428c1. Kate's own label: 'provisional, schema-neutral drafts derived from the supplied task, not additions to Zach's authorization'; she had the handoff only, not the source. Committed verbatim by claude:anamnesis#wake-20261118-02; not accepted by Zach. Kate's id: comparator-independent-03. Kate's acceptance text: \"A reviewer can trace each classification to its evidence and distinguish when events occurred from when they were observed.\"", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-DCK-4", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Consumer acceptance requires a named recipient's acknowledgement and substantive row-specific disposition, checked outside the producer-consumer pair, within a window fixed before observation.", "authored_by": "chatgpt:kate", "author_role": "independent", "rationale": "relay-kit-private kate-replies:replies/HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1--6b3fa1a21995.md (API Kate, gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-11-18T01:56:56Z), ask 6b3fa1a21995 on HO-ANA-20261117-2VK1; targets Anamnesis#13 at b2428c1. Kate's own label: 'provisional, schema-neutral drafts derived from the supplied task, not additions to Zach's authorization'; she had the handoff only, not the source. Committed verbatim by claude:anamnesis#wake-20261118-02; not accepted by Zach. Kate's id: comparator-independent-04. Kate's acceptance text: \"Record the acknowledgement, dispositions, independent check, window start, eligible wakes, and wall-cap outcome.\"", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-ENG-4", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Where an instance's index lives is a backend choice behind one interface (fetch, destination, publish); every built index is keyed by a digest of its sources and schema, so a stale index is rebuilt rather than served, and a build is atomic. The engine ships local backends only; which option an instance uses is Zach's choice", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261119-05", "author_role": "implementer", "rationale": "HO-ANA-20261118-6H0J item 3 (DEC-252; Zach 2026-11-18 10:52 CT: \"any use of CogScaff needs to be quick. Whether that means the indices and embedded vectors in GitHub or hosted somewhere else is another question\"). Measurements and recommendation: docs/research/index-storage.md. Tested by tests/test_storage.py", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-ENG-5", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "An answer is extractive and cited: every line quotes one message unit and names its message_unit_id, speaker, conversation and branch; the active path is searched first and alternates only when it has no hit, labelled as not the chosen reply; a question with no matching source gets no answer rather than a guess", "authored_by": "claude:anamnesis#wake-20261119-13", "author_role": "implementer", "rationale": "HO-ANA-20261118-6H0J item 4 (cold test steps 3-4: ingest a synthetic ChatGPT export, ask a question and get an answer that cites a source). Engine-level only; CLI and instance wiring follow Anamnesis#15/#16. Tested by tests/test_answer.py", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "serves", "to": "R-ENG-2@1"}]}